.TH SYSCALL_MONITOR 1 "September 2026" "ebpf-syscall" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
syscall_monitor \- capture and summarize filesystem-related system calls
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B syscall_monitor
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B syscall_monitor
uses eBPF tracepoints to observe filesystem and IO system calls.  It can keep
aggregate statistics or retain detailed events and export the result as JSON
for later inspection or replay.
.PP
The program normally offers interactive choices.  Use
.B \-\-duration
and
.B \-\-no-prompt
for an unattended capture.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-max-events " number"
Limit retained detailed events.  The default is 1,000,000.  The program
reports events discarded after the buffer reaches this limit.
.TP
.BI \-\-duration " seconds"
Stop after the given time instead of waiting for interactive termination.
.TP
.B \-\-detailed
Enable per-event ring-buffer logging.
.TP
.B \-\-no-detailed
Disable per-event logging and retain aggregate information only.
.TP
.BI \-\-json-out " path"
Write JSON to the given path and do not prompt for an export destination.
.TP
.BI \-\-label " name"
Store a workload label in the JSON metadata.
.TP
.B \-\-no-prompt
Skip all interactive prompts and use command-line defaults.
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Show usage.
.SH PRIVACY
Detailed output can contain process names, file names, descriptors, offsets,
sizes, and timing.  It does not copy file payloads, but this metadata can still
identify users, files, and access patterns.  Review it before sharing.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR syscall_replayer (1),
.BR kvio (1)
